WHAT THE CC0 DEDICATION IN LICENSE COVERS

It covers the DATA in this repository: the station records, the schema, the
index and the generated playlists. Public domain, no attribution required.

IT DOES NOT COVER THE AUDIO STREAMS THE URLs POINT AT

Those are operated by third-party broadcasters. They are not ours, they are
not ours to license, and they may be geo-blocked, rate-limited, moved or
withdrawn at any time.

A "verified" date means the stream answered with audio bytes on that day. It
is a statement about reachability and nothing else -- not an endorsement, not
a claim about who owns the audio, and not a grant of any right to rebroadcast
it. If you intend to redistribute a stream rather than link to it, that is
between you and the broadcaster.

WHAT IS DELIBERATELY NOT HERE

Nothing in this repository is derived from a share-alike or otherwise
restrictive source, and that is enforced rather than intended: the generator
publishes station fields from an allowlist and STOPS if it meets a field
nobody has classified, because a licence that depends on no one having made a
mistake is a claim and not a fact.

In particular, transmitter coordinates from OpenStreetMap are ODbL
(share-alike) and are excluded. Where globalradio.app uses such data it keeps
it in a separate place under its own licence. Broadcast frequencies here are
read off the stations' own names and are plain fact.

SOURCE

Station discovery comes from Radio Browser (https://www.radio-browser.info),
a community directory whose collected data its author placed in the public
domain. Attribution is not required by either project and is the right thing
to do anyway: the directory exists only because people kept adding to it.

Verification, filtering, normalisation and the schema are the work of
globalradio.app (https://globalradio.app).
